e departure of f(R) from linearity. The bound that we find for f″ (0) is so huge that permit almost any f(R). This is in the nature of things: the effect of higher order terms in f(R) are strongly suppressed by power of Planck's time 8πG 0. In order to improve these bounds more research on mathematical aspects of these theories and experimental consequences is necessary.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Springer"}}],"refereed":true,"titles":[{"title":"f(R) cosmology in the first order formalism"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"$f(R)$ cosmology in the first order formalism"}],"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"SPIRES","value":"SPIRES-4872444"},{"schema":"MSNET","value":"1908589"}],"facet_author_name":["984391_Hector Vucetich","1006854_Victor H. Hamity","1045816_D.E. Barraco"],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:583145","updated":"2025-06-06T17:49:11.514212"},"curated":true,"journal_title_variants":["Gen.Rel.Grav.","Gen. Rel. Grav."]},"id":"583145","updated":"2025-06-06T17:49:11.514212+00:00","created":"2002-12-03T00:00:00+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/583145?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/583145?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/583145?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/583145?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/583145?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/583145?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A583145"}},{"metadata":{"citation_count_without_self_citations":24,"authors":[{"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/056tb7j80"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"barraco, d.e.","full_name":"Barraco, D.E.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1045816"},"last_name":"Barraco","affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/904339"},"value":"Cordo